 "_readme": "ROUND 1 of the NR4A3-fusion cistrome search (2026-08-08). Every entry is a JSON API endpoint, so lit_fetch_urls.py writes the payload byte-for-byte. Purpose: settle whether ANY genome-wide chromatin/binding experiment involving an NR4A3 fusion (EWSR1::NR4A3, TAF15::NR4A3, TCF12::NR4A3, FUS::NR4A3, HSPA8::NR4A3) or NR4A3 in a sarcoma context has been deposited in a public archive. The prior repository search (research/modalities/emc-ret-cistrome.json) was ANTIGEN-CENTRIC \u2014 antigen in {NR4A1,NR4A2,NR4A3} only \u2014 and therefore could not see a fusion ChIP labelled by its 5' partner or by an epitope tag, an ATAC/CUT&RUN/DNase experiment of any kind, or a deposit indexed only in SRA/BioProject/ENA. This corpus closes those. Keys prefixed 'ctrl_' are KNOWN-POSITIVE CONTROLS: each must return a non-zero count, or that archive's zero is a transport failure rather than an absence.",
